# BPFLab website — Astro environment variables.
# Copy to `website/.env`; Astro loads it for both `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build`.
# Only variables prefixed with PUBLIC_ are available to browser code.

# Base URL of the execution backend the editor posts C source to.
#   dev (`pnpm dev`):    unset -> http://localhost:8081 (the Compose backend's
#                        loopback listener). If you change BACKEND_PORT in the
#                        root .env, set this to match, e.g.
#                        PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9081
#   build (`pnpm build`): unset -> same-origin "" (nginx proxies /run_code/)
# Setting it for a production build points the editor at that absolute URL;
# the backend must then allow that origin (its CORS defaults to
# localhost/127.0.0.1 only). See README "Environment variables".
#PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8081
